p.src:
In quantum mechanics the angular part of a state with definite orbital angular momentum is a spherical harmonic. Write the separated state as $\Psi_{n_r\ell m}(r,\theta,\phi)
=\frac{u_{n_r\ell}(r)}{r}\,
Y_{\ell m}(\theta,\phi).$ The angular operator $L^2$ has the eigenvalue $L^2Y_{\ell m}
=\hbar^2\ell(\ell+1)Y_{\ell m}.$ For a fixed pair $n_r,\ell$, abbreviate $u_{n_r\ell}(r)$ to $u(r)$. The equation left for the reduced radial function is $\begin{aligned}
&-\frac{\hbar^2}{2m}\frac{d^2u}{dr^2}
+\frac{\hbar^2\ell(\ell+1)}{2mr^2}u(r)\\
&\qquad+V(r)u(r)=E_{n_r\ell}\,u(r).
\end{aligned}$

